When a reused implementation subagent has accumulated a very large context (hundreds of k tokens), spawn a fresh agent with a concise handoff brief (current HEAD, relevant files, decisions, task) instead of resuming it.

**Why:** The user asked (2026-10-11) that the subagent "compact its memory before working" after the long-lived web-UI agent got slow and was cut off mid-task by limits.

**How to apply:** Before each new sprint, judge the reused agent's context size; if large, write a short brief and start a new agent. Still mention reading CLAUDE.md and the no-nested-subagents rule. Related: [[orchestrator-subagent-reuse]]

